        "recommendation": "#1: stable terminal task names. This is a relatively contained improvement that makes concurrent work easier to identify and supports later search and activity features.",
        "options": [],
        "required": false,
        "preview": {
          "html": "<style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:16px;background:#19191f;color:#f2f1f6;font:15px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}h2{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 16px;color:#b8b6c4;font-size:13px}.ideas{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:9px}.idea{display:flex;gap:12px;padding:14px;border:1px solid #45434f;border-radius:9px;cursor:pointer;background:#232229}.idea:hover{border-color:#a393d9}.idea:has(input:checked){border-color:#bcacff;background:#312941;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #bcacff}.idea:focus-within{outline:2px solid #bcacff;outline-offset:2px}input{accent-color:#c5b3ff;width:17px;height:17px;flex-shrink:0;margin:3px 0 0}.copy{min-width:0}.title{display:block;font-size:15px;font-weight:650}.num{color:#c8b7ff}.desc{display:block;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4;color:#ceccd7;margin-top:5px}.scope{display:block;color:#a9a5b8;font-size:12px;margin-top:7px}#selection{margin-top:16px;color:#d4c8ff;font-size:14px} @media(min-width:640px){.ideas{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}\n</style><h2>Choose one proposal</h2><p>All 15 ideas are listed individually in the report’s original order. Scope labels are relative, not time estimates.</p><div class=\"ideas\"><label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"1\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">1.</span> Stable task names for individual terminals</span><span class=\"desc\">Give each terminal a lasting task name, so several agents are easy to tell apart.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: S–M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"2\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">2.</span> Searchable workspace switcher</span><span class=\"desc\">Search spaces, groups and terminals, then jump directly to the right pane.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"3\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">3.</span> Activity overview and next-unread navigation</span><span class=\"desc\">See what needs attention and move through unread work across spaces.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"4\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">4.</span> Local control API, CLI and agent guide</span><span class=\"desc\">Let agents inspect and operate Chartr through a documented local interface.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: L; small initial API</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"5\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">5.</span> Reusable workspace recipes</span><span class=\"desc\">Recreate a useful arrangement of agents, terminals and project tools in one action.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M–L</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"6\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">6.</span> Pane zoom and keyboard resizing</span><span class=\"desc\">Temporarily enlarge a pane and adjust splits without losing the arrangement.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: S–M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"7\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">7.</span> Set aside running work</span><span class=\"desc\">Tuck away a live terminal to reduce clutter, then find and restore it later.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"8\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">8.</span> Named jobs with reliable completion and retained failures</span><span class=\"desc\">Give tests and builds a name, record their actual exit result and retain failures for review.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M–L</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"9\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">9.</span> Terminal capture and export</span><span class=\"desc\">Capture designated terminal output for sharing, diagnosis or agent inspection.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"10\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">10.</span> Path picker and directory-aware launches</span><span class=\"desc\">Insert paths safely and start new terminals in the intended working directory.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"11\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">11.</span> Settings search and shortcut explanations</span><span class=\"desc\">Find settings quickly and understand which shortcut mapping takes effect.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"12\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">12.</span> Resource budgets for background terminals</span><span class=\"desc\">Measure large-workspace costs, then reduce proven CPU, memory or rendering overhead.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: Measure first</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"13\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">13.</span> Session/backend diagnostics and update state</span><span class=\"desc\">See session health and running backend versions, with useful recovery diagnostics.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"14\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">14.</span> Optional explicit program-status input</span><span class=\"desc\">Let programs report progress, blocked reasons and child work through structured signals.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: L; backend-dependent</span></span></label>\n<label class=\"idea\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proposal\" value=\"15\"><span class=\"copy\"><span class=\"title\"><span class=\"num\">15.</span> Discoverable plugin commands</span><span class=\"desc\">Expose project-tool actions in the command palette and through automation.</span><span class=\"scope\">Scope: M–L</span></span></label></div><p id=\"selection\" role=\"status\">No proposal selected.</p><script>\nconst titles={\"1\": \"Stable task names for individual terminals\", \"2\": \"Searchable workspace switcher\", \"3\": \"Activity overview and next-unread navigation\", \"4\": \"Local control API, CLI and agent guide\", \"5\": \"Reusable workspace recipes\", \"6\": \"Pane zoom and keyboard resizing\", \"7\": \"Set aside running work\", \"8\": \"Named jobs with reliable completion and retained failures\", \"9\": \"Terminal capture and export\", \"10\": \"Path picker and directory-aware launches\", \"11\": \"Settings search and shortcut explanations\", \"12\": \"Resource budgets for background terminals\", \"13\": \"Session/backend diagnostics and update state\", \"14\": \"Optional explicit program-status input\", \"15\": \"Discoverable plugin commands\"};\nconst radios=[...document.querySelectorAll('input[name=\"proposal\"]')];\nfunction draw(){const chosen=grill.state.primaryProposal;for(const radio of radios)radio.checked=Number(radio.value)===chosen;document.getElementById('selection').textContent=chosen?'Selected: #'+chosen+' '+titles[chosen]:'No proposal selected.';}\nfor(const radio of radios)radio.addEventListener('change',()=>{if(radio.checked){const n=Number(radio.value);grill.setState({primaryProposal:n,primaryTitle:titles[n]});draw();}});\ndraw();\n</script>",
